  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="detail">
        <p>In January 1918, <ref target="http://nla.gov.au/nla.news-article232463401">Alexander</ref> and <ref target="http://nla.gov.au/nla.news-article232463395">Nathan</ref> Kurcick of 172 Bouverie Street changed their surname to Carrick [Commonwealth of Australia Gazette].</p>
        <p>The same year, there is a file in the national Archives (yet to be consulted) which mentions the two:</p>
        <quote>
          <p>Kurcick, Alexander and Nathan (Otherwise Carrick), 1918</p>
          <p>World War I Intelligence section case files, annual single number series, <ref target="https://recordsearch.naa.gov.au/SearchNRetrieve/Interface/DetailsReports/SeriesDetail.aspx?series_no=MP16/1&amp;singleRecord=T">NAA: MP16/1, 1918/55, ID 320186</ref></p>
        </quote>
      </div>
    </body>
